"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JZJY8NY61S0RH07\",\"title\":\"Darjeeling Revival: Monsoon Harvest — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"VALIDATED\",\"EW\",\"1,000Y+\",\"Darjeeling Revival: Monsoon Harvest\",\"Alt Carbon\",\"ISSUED\",\"6,579.94\",\"BUFFER POOL\",\"131.6\",\"CREDITING PERIOD\",\"01 Oct 2024 to 01 Oct 2029\",\"Summary\"],\"issued_header\":\"6,579.94\",\"buffer_header\":\"131.6\",\"crediting\":\"01 Oct 2024 to 01 Oct 2029\",\"verifier\":\"350Solutions\",\"code\":\"SD0E\",\"approval\":\"29 Apr 2026\",\"protocol_current\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":\"6,579.94\",\"cert_retired\":\"919\",\"cert_buffer\":\"131.6\",\"reversal\":\"The risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Alt Carbon's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 131.6 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 191.335 certificates.\\n\\nAlt Carbon has no reversals to date.\",\"showing\":[\"Showing 1 of 1\",\"Showing 5 of 5\",\"Showing 1 of 1\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Name\",\"Category\",\"Validated\"],\"rows\":[[\"DRP2_Basalt\",\"Mineral & rock\",\"20 May 2026\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"29 Apr 2026\",\"Verification Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"29 Apr 2026\",\"GHG Statement Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"14 Jan 2026\",\"Validation Report\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"06 Oct 2025\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"01 Sep 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]},{\"heads\":[\"Issue date\",\"Issued\",\"Buffer pool\",\"Supplier allocation\"],\"rows\":[[\"29 Apr 2026\",\"6,579.94\",\"131.6\",\"6,448.34\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE\",\"t\":\"Alt Carbon\"},{\"h\":\"https://350solutions.com\",\"t\":\"350Solutions\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/enhanced-weathering-agriculture/1.1\",\"t\":\"Enhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JZJY8NY61S0RH07/pjd_1KQDDAV0R1S0F9EM/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 01 Sep 2025\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KP3N5DC81S0TCV7?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JZJY8NY61S0RH07/pjd_1KZCCJDTH1S0JQX4/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JZJY8NY61S0RH07/pjd_1KQDHW6531S0P7NW/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JZJY8NY61S0RH07/pjd_1KZCCGDHW1S0BE5T/validation_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JZJY8NY61S0RH07/pjd_1K6WAKNVB1S09SCK/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1J6EQFMYF1S00KDE/prj_1JZJY8NY61S0RH07/pjd_1KQDDAV0R1S0F9EM/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nEW\\n1,000Y+\\nDarjeeling Revival: Monsoon Harvest\\nAlt Carbon\\nISSUED\\n6,579.94\\nBUFFER POOL\\n131.6\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Oct 2024 to 01 Oct 2029\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nCalculation overview\\nFeedstocks\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nThe project is primarily focused on the Terai region, leveraging the high rainfall, warm summers, and collaboration with local tea growers. The project enhances soil health and crop productivity while sequestering atmospheric CO₂. This approach aids in carbon removal and supports the local economy, preserves biodiversity, and promotes sustainable agricultural practices.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nSD0E\\nApproval date\\n29 Apr 2026\\nCurrent protocol version\\nEnhanced Weathering in Agriculture v1.1\\nSUSTAINABLE DEVELOPMENT GOALS\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nDarjeeling Revival: Monsoon Harvest\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nEnhanced Weathering (EW) accelerates the Earth's natural chemical weathering process to remove carbon dioxide from the atmosphere. In chemical weathering, carbon dioxide dissolved in rainwater reacts with minerals in rocks, partly dissolving them and producing stable bicarbonate ions. These bicarbonate ions are transported by rivers to the ocean, where they are safely stored for thousands of years. EW is typically carried out by spreading crushed reactive rocks or minerals on croplands.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n01 Sep 2025\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 3,745.26 tCO₂e removed from Darjeeling Revival: Monsoon Harvest on 14 Oct 2025\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n3,745.262 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n4,248.882 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n503.620 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nFeedstocks\\n\\nFeedstocks are the validated input materials that have been used for this project.\\n\\nName\\tCategory\\tValidated\\nDRP2_Basalt\\tMineral & rock\\t20 May 2026\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n29 Apr 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n29 Apr 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n14 Jan 2026\\tValidation Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n06 Oct 2025\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n01 Sep 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 5\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n6,579.94\\nRetired\\n919\\nBuffer pool\\n131.6\\nCrediting period\\n01 Oct 2024 to 01 Oct 2029\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n29 Apr 2026\\t6,579.94\\t131.6\\t6,448.34\\nShowing 1 of 1\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Alt Carbon's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 131.6 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 191.335 certificates.\\n\\nAlt Carbon has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"